  {
    "name": "close-during-an-in-flight-start",
    "axis": "close",
    "why": "round-3 blocker 2: the attempt must not outlive close(), and a start that observes a closed runtime must FAIL",
    "projection": {
      "values": { "policy.mode": "static-value" },
      "varSources": { "svc": { "transport": "fake" } },
      "vars": { "policy": { "source": "svc", "mode": "prefetch" } },
      "schema": { "var.policy.mode": { "type": "string" } }
    },
    "source": {
      "policy": {
        "kind": "head",
        "generation": 1,
        "revision": "sha256:r1",
        "effectiveAt": "2026-07-20T00:00:00Z",
        "values": { "policy.mode": "v1" }
      }
    },
    "steps": [
      { "action": "blockPull", "scope": "policy" },
      { "action": "startAsync" },
      { "action": "awaitPullIssued", "scope": "policy", "count": 1, "timeoutMs": 3000 },
      { "action": "closeAsync" },
      {
        "action": "expect",
        "status": "divergent",
        "note": "DIVERGENCE-4: whether close() can CANCEL an in-flight prefetch. Go derives the prefetch ctx from the runtime ctx, so close() aborts the pull and returns promptly. The Node provider contract (`pull(scope, knownRevision): Promise<...>`) carries no cancellation signal at all, and VarManager.close() awaits the start attempt BEFORE closing providers, so close() blocks until the in-flight pull settles on its own. Both satisfy the ADR clause 'close() does not return until the attempt has stopped'; the ADR's parenthetical ('Node's providers are closed and the attempt re-checked') describes an intent the shipped code does not implement, and honoring it needs a provider-contract change.",
        "adr": "docs/cnos-runtime-vars.md - 'Startup / close lifecycle (canonical, both SDKs)'",
        "observed": {
          "node": { "closeSettledWithinMs": 400, "settled": false },
          "go": { "closeSettledWithinMs": 400, "settled": true }
        }
      },
      { "action": "releasePull", "scope": "policy" },
      { "action": "awaitClose" },
      { "action": "awaitStart" },
      { "action": "expect", "startOutcome": "error", "startErrorKind": "closed" },
      { "action": "expect", "closeOutcome": "ok" }
    ]
  },
